# The fleet's lanes - generated by scripts/lanes from fleet-kit/lanes/*.toml, do not edit.
# Installed as /opt/cti-agent/share/lanes.list. FLEET_LANES names lanes from here.
# lane<TAB>units<TAB>credential checks run-credcheck runs for it (- for none)<TAB>programs its units start<TAB>summary
checkin	checkin,credcheck	cti-mailer,cti-jira	run-checkin,run-credcheck	The orchestrator's heartbeat: one /checkin beat of the Claude Code agent that watches the other lanes.
digest	digest,weekly	-	run-digest	The daily threat-intel digest: read the CTI mail, enrich every CVE with exposure on our hosts, and send the brief; on Mondays, the weekly rollup.
scout	scout	-	cti-scout	Poll advisory feeds for CVEs the mail has not mentioned yet, to feed the digest.
patchtuesday	patchtuesday	-	run-patchtuesday	The monthly Microsoft Patch Tuesday synopsis, with exposure on our hosts. Run by hand for now; its timer is off on purpose.
appscan	appscan	cti-appreport	run-appscan	The weekly application-security report from the web app scanner's results, with Jira tickets per application.
appowners	appowners	-	run-appowners	Each application's scan report, sent to its owners the morning after the scan.
domains	domains	cti-domains	run-domains	The weekly domains check: registrar, DNS, web and mail records, plus one Jira ticket for IT.
vmscan	vmscan	cti-vmscan	run-vmscan	The weekly VM scan report: which scheduled scans ran, and which networks in the network sheet no scan reached.
supplier	supplier	-	run-supplier	Supplier requests from the supplier mailbox, judged for third-party risk, with Jira Kanban items.
mailbox	mailbox	-	run-mailbox-cleanup	Mailbox housekeeping: file processed advisories away after the digest has read them.
